draft: true
id: E554
title: Inject a Conan CMake install contract for Makefile-only C++ libraries
scope: conan cmake makefile ohos package install headers static shared
symptoms: An upstream C++ library has only a Makefile with hard-coded host compilers and no install target, so Conan cannot produce a reproducible OHOS package.
root_cause: The upstream build assumes a native GNU environment and leaves compiler selection, library installation, and public headers outside a package contract.
repair: Add a minimal task-owned CMakeLists that lists the upstream sources, exposes shared and fPIC options, uses Conan's toolchain, installs the public headers and target, and maps cpp_info to the observed archive and exported target.
verification: TinyXML 2.6.2 upstream Makefile built xmltest with 109/109 checks; Conan OHOS armv8 create built libtinyxml.a and the consumer linked successfully; Windows host consumer returned PASS.
boundaries: Applies to small self-contained Makefile libraries; retain upstream source and test inventory, and do not treat cross-built consumer compilation as target runtime evidence.
